---
layout: layout.njk
pagination:
  data: events
  size: 1
  alias: event
# D-19: `event_id` IS `edition_code`, lower-cased -- nothing else names an
# event. `events.json`'s own `id` column carries `edition_code` verbatim,
# not lower-cased (`tools/convener_ops/public_data.py::PUBLIC_FIELD_SOURCES`),
# so the lower-casing happens here, once, the same rule `platform.find_speaker`
# and `registration.signup_url` already apply on the Python side. This is
# the *whole* address: never derived from the title, which changes when a
# speaker's talk is retitled and would move the page a QR code or a shared
# link already points at.
permalink: "/events/{{ event.id | lower }}/"
---

{% set isUpcoming = event.status == "scheduled" %}

<section class="hero event-lead">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="event-lead__back">
      <a href="/" class="unstyled">&larr; All editions</a>
    </p>
    <article class="feature">
      <aside class="feature__rail">
        <p class="feature__vol">{% if isUpcoming %}Upcoming{% else %}Past edition{% endif %}</p>
        <p class="feature__code">{{ event.id }}</p>
        <p class="feature__date">
          <strong>{{ event.date }}</strong><br>
          12:30 CET
        </p>
      </aside>
      <div class="feature__body">
        <h1 class="feature__title">{{ event.title }}</h1>
        <p class="feature__speaker">
          {{ event.speaker_name }}{% if event.speaker_affiliation %}<span class="feature__affil"> &middot; {{ event.speaker_affiliation }}</span>{% endif %}
        </p>
        {% if event.abstract %}
        <p class="feature__abstract">{{ event.abstract }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container">
  <header class="section__head">
    <span class="section__num">01</span>
    <span class="section__label">Recording &amp; discussion</span>
  </header>

  <div class="archive__actions event__links">
    {% if event.youtube_url %}
      <a class="archive__action unstyled" href="{{ event.youtube_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="archive__action--disabled">No recording yet</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% if event.forum_thread %}
      <a class="archive__action archive__action--alt unstyled" href="{{ event.forum_thread }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discuss</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="archive__action--disabled">No thread yet</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{% if isUpcoming %}
<section class="section container">
  <header class="section__head">
    <span class="section__num">02</span>
    <span class="section__label">Register</span>
  </header>

  {#
    Phase 4 spec section 4 ("Formalities"): a one-screen notice on the
    event page, before the form. The wording below is the one phase 4
    already settled and shipped, originally at `app/src/signup/
    SignupForm.tsx`'s own `Notice()` component (quoted here at task 5,
    rather than redrafted). Task 6 removed that component's own copy once
    it mounted the registration island beneath this notice: D-18 keeps
    text that needs no interactivity as plain static HTML, so this block
    is now the *only* copy, not a second one kept in step with a first --
    see `app/src/islands/signup/SignupForm.tsx`'s own module comment.
    `tools/tests/test_confirmation.py` still pins the retention figure
    ("90 days") across this page, `confirmation.py` and the docs copy, and
    `tools/tests/test_site.py` pins the contact address below against
    `confirmation.CONTACT_EMAIL` -- so neither the wording nor the address
    can quietly drift from those.
  #}
  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">Before you register</p>
    <p>
      We collect your first name, surname and email address to register you for
      this event and to issue your attendance certificate afterwards. Institution
      is optional. Nothing else is asked for.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your browser encrypts this information before it is sent</strong>,
      using this event&rsquo;s own key. Nobody &mdash; including us &mdash; can
      read it until an organiser decrypts it as part of running the event. The
      event&rsquo;s data, encrypted form included, is permanently destroyed
      90 days after the event by destroying the key that could ever read it
      again.
    </p>
    <p>
      To access, correct or erase your data before that date, write to
      <a href="mailto:reading-group@example.test">reading-group@example.test</a>.
      Read the full
      <a href="https://github.com/example-instance/example-cockpit/blob/main/docs/governance/traitement-donnees.md">data-protection record</a>
      for what we hold, why, and for how long.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#
    Task 6: the registration island itself, mounted here, beneath this
    notice -- extracted from the operators' application into its own
    small, self-contained bundle, so a visitor who wants to register never
    downloads the cockpit (D-18's own argument). Nothing renders
    `event.registration_link` anywhere on this page, or anywhere else in
    this site: the room link is delivered only by the confirmation
    e-mail, never published (acceptance criterion 2).

    `#registration-form` is `app/src/islands/signup/main.tsx`'s own mount
    point -- kept as the exact id task 5 already reserved and
    `tools/tests/test_site.py::test_the_notice_precedes_the_reserved_
    place_for_the_registration_form` already pins, so that test needed no
    change here. `data-event-id` is how the island learns which event
    it is on: one static page per event (D-19), not a route param this
    script re-parses. The element starts empty; `signup.js` fills it in,
    which is exactly why the `<noscript>` fallback beside it exists --
    without JavaScript, nothing here would ever render at all.
  #}
  <div id="registration-form" data-event-id="{{ event.id | lower }}"></div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="notice">
      Registering needs JavaScript enabled. If you cannot enable it, write to
      <a href="mailto:reading-group@example.test">reading-group@example.test</a>
      and we will register you by hand.
    </p>
  </noscript>
  <script type="module" src="/app/islands/signup/signup.js"></script>
</section>
{% endif %}
